  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis is adjacent to https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2272 but focus more on the [flow content that is permitted inside `<details>`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#dom-dialog-open).\n\nLooking at [WCAG 4.1.2 Success Criteria](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/#name-role-value) nesting interactive elements (such as `<a>`) should be avoided. [You don't do that with `<button>`](https://accessibilityinsights.io/info-examples/web/nested-interactive/) for example.\n\nI'm confused as the WHATWG also has an example with form controls inside a `<details>`.\n\nWhat is the most accessible approach here?",
